IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cea-types`
IMPORT `cea-dates`
IMPORT `cea-value`
IMPORT `cea-duty`
IMPORT `cea-refunds`
IMPORT `cea-goal`

-- Independent tests, written from independent-expectations.md (scenario ids
-- in the comments). Expected values come from the Act, not the encoding.

`Matariki` MEANS LIST Date 10 7 2026, Date 25 6 2027, Date 14 7 2028

`nobody` MEANS `Buyer and seller` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

-- A plain transaction: price, no cl 5 problems, unrelated, no adjustments.
GIVEN price IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Transaction facts`
`plain` price MEANS
    `Transaction facts` OF price, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, `nobody`, TRUE, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, 0, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY

-- A transaction with additions and deductions.
GIVEN price IS A NUMBER
      adds IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      deds IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A `Transaction facts`
`adjusted` price adds deds MEANS
    `Transaction facts` OF price, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, `nobody`, TRUE, adds, FALSE, deds, 0, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY

-- A transaction whose cl 5 test fails (restriction), with comparables.
GIVEN ident IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      simil IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A `Transaction facts`
`failing` ident simil MEANS
    `Transaction facts` OF 10000, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, `nobody`, TRUE, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, 0, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, ident, simil

GIVEN occ IS A `Payment occasion`, od IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`due` occ od MEANS `the payment date for` (`Duty facts` OF occ, od, NOTHING, EMPTY) `, Matariki days` `Matariki`

-- s 113 duty 10,000, notice 2 Nov 2026 (PD 30 Nov 2026), with payments.
GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF Payment
GIVETH A NUMBER
`pen113` ps MEANS `the late payment penalties on duty of` 10000 `, facts` (`Duty facts` OF `s 124(3) an assessment under s 113`, Date 2 11 2026, NOTHING, ps) `, Matariki days` `Matariki` `, as at` (Date 31 12 2027)

GIVEN occ IS A `Payment occasion`, od IS A DATE, dfr IS A MAYBE DATE, duty IS A NUMBER
      ps IS A LIST OF Payment
GIVETH A NUMBER
`pen` occ od dfr duty ps MEANS `the late payment penalties on duty of` duty `, facts` (`Duty facts` OF occ, od, dfr, ps) `, Matariki days` `Matariki` `, as at` (Date 31 12 2027)

GIVEN paidOn IS A DATE, appl IS A MAYBE DATE, cons IS A DATE, err IS A BOOLEAN, gr IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- [Ported by the encoder: `Refund facts` gained `refund Matariki days` (s 55), given as EMPTY; no expected value changed.]
`refund` paidOn appl cons err gr MEANS `the duty must be refunded` (`Refund facts` OF EMPTY, paidOn, appl, cons, err, gr)

-- ===== Goal 1: related persons (cl 2(2)) =====
-- R1
#ASSERT `are related` (`Buyer and seller` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
-- R2
#ASSERT `are related` (`Buyer and seller` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
-- R3
#ASSERT `are related` (`Buyer and seller` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
-- R4 (exactly 5%)
#ASSERT `are related` (`Buyer and seller` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 5, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
-- R5 (4.99% of one, 60% of the other: the share of both is 4.99)
#ASSERT NOT `are related` (`Buyer and seller` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 4.99, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
-- R7
#ASSERT `are related` (`Buyer and seller` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
-- R8
#ASSERT `are related` (`Buyer and seller` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)
-- R9
#ASSERT `are related` (`Buyer and seller` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE)
-- R10 / R12 / R13 / R14 / R15 (family, one input)
#ASSERT `are related` (`Buyer and seller` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE)
-- R16
#ASSERT NOT `are related` `nobody`

-- ===== Goal 1: clause 5 =====
-- C1
#ASSERT `the transaction value can be used` (`plain` 10000)
-- C5
#ASSERT NOT `the transaction value can be used` (`Transaction facts` OF 10000, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, `nobody`, TRUE, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, 0, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY)
-- C6
#ASSERT NOT `the transaction value can be used` (`Transaction facts` OF 10000, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, `nobody`, TRUE, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, 0, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY)
-- C9
#ASSERT NOT `the transaction value can be used` (`Transaction facts` OF 10000, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, `nobody`, TRUE, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, 0, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY)
-- C10 / C11 (related, cl 6 complied with or not required)
#ASSERT `the transaction value can be used` (`Transaction facts` OF 10000, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, (`Buyer and seller` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), TRUE, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, 0, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY)
-- C12 (related, required, not complied)
#ASSERT NOT `the transaction value can be used` (`Transaction facts` OF 10000, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, (`Buyer and seller` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, 0, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY)
-- C12 variant: not related, clause 6 flag false is irrelevant
#ASSERT `the transaction value can be used` (`Transaction facts` OF 10000, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, `nobody`, FALSE, EMPTY, FALSE, EMPTY, 0, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY)

-- ===== Goal 1: clause 7 transaction value =====
